# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISTRIBUTION BOUNDARY
# This repo ships timestamps and code. It never ships source media.
# These rules exist before the exporter does, deliberately. Do not relax them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Video / audio, in any form, anywhere in the tree
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mov
*.ts
*.m2ts
*.webm
*.mp3
*.aac
*.ac3
*.flac
*.wav
*.dts

# Frames, thumbnails, contact sheets — not as docs images, not as test output
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp

# Subtitles extracted from source rips (user's own media, not ours to ship)
*.srt
*.ass
*.ssa
*.sub
*.idx
*.vtt

# Exporter working areas
segments/
out/
scratch/
*.concat

# Local machine state — calibration is per-library, never committed
cache/
offsets.local.*
media-map.local.*

# Generated playlists. These embed absolute paths into someone's media library
# and timestamps calibrated to it, so they are machine-specific output, not
# publishable artifacts. The scene list YAML *is* publishable — it stays in
# dataset time — so it is deliberately not excluded here.
*.edl
*.m3u
*.m3u8

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
